#: ../../solid/polarization.rst:5
msgid "周期結晶の分極"
msgstr "Polarization in Periodic Crystals"

#: ../../solid/polarization.rst:7
msgid ""
"\\ :ref:`自発分極<spontaneous-polarization>`\\ は単位体積あたりの電気双極子モーメントだが、周期結晶では、単位胞の中の電荷の "
"双極子を体積で割るだけでは値が一つに決まらない。本稿では、1次元のイオン鎖でこの不定性を確かめ、分極の量子と、 "
"反転対称な構造の分極を説明する。続いて、原子の変位から分極を見積もるBorn有効電荷と、分極を電子状態から求める Berry位相の方法の概要を扱い、正方晶BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ "
"の分極を見積もる。"
msgstr ""
"\\ :ref:`Spontaneous polarization <spontaneous-polarization>`\\  is the electric dipole moment "
"per unit volume. In a periodic crystal, the value obtained by dividing the dipole moment of the "
"charges in a unit cell by its volume depends on the choice of cell. We illustrate this ambiguity "
"with a one-dimensional ionic chain, then explain the polarization quantum and polarization in "
"inversion-symmetric structures. We introduce the Born effective charge for estimating "
"polarization from atomic displacements and the Berry phase method for obtaining it from the "
"electronic states. We use these ideas to estimate the polarization of tetragonal BaTiO\\ "
":sub:`3`\\ ."

#: ../../solid/polarization.rst:12
msgid "本稿で扱うのは、占有バンドと非占有バンドの間にバンドギャップが開いた絶縁体である。金属では伝導電子が電場を遮蔽するので、 巨視的な分極は定義されない。"
msgstr ""
"This article concerns insulators with a band gap between the occupied and unoccupied bands. In "
"metals, conduction electrons screen the electric field, so macroscopic polarization is undefined."

#: ../../solid/polarization.rst:15
msgid ""
"**前提知識**: :ref:`自発分極<spontaneous-polarization>`、:ref:`反転対称性と自発分極<inversion-and-polarization>`、 "
":ref:`ブロッホの定理<bloch-theorem>`、:ref:`第1ブリルアンゾーン<first-brillouin-zone>`。"
msgstr ""
"**Prerequisites**: :ref:`Spontaneous Polarization <spontaneous-polarization>`, :ref:`Inversion "
"Symmetry and Spontaneous Polarization <inversion-and-polarization>`, :ref:`Bloch’s Theorem "
"<bloch-theorem>`, and :ref:`First Brillouin Zone <first-brillouin-zone>`."

#: ../../solid/polarization.rst:18
msgid "**学習目標**:"
msgstr "**Learning objectives**:"

#: ../../solid/polarization.rst:20
msgid "周期結晶の分極が分極の量子の整数倍だけ不定であることを1次元の鎖で導き、反転対称な構造の分極が0か分極の量子の半分になることを説明する。"
msgstr ""
"Use a one-dimensional chain to derive why polarization in a periodic crystal is defined only up "
"to an integer multiple of the polarization quantum. Explain why the polarization of an inversion-"
"symmetric structure is zero or half a polarization quantum modulo that quantum."

#: ../../solid/polarization.rst:21
msgid "Born有効電荷を定義し、原子の変位から分極を見積もる。形式電荷との違いを数値で示す。"
msgstr ""
"Define the Born effective charge and use atomic displacements to estimate polarization. Quantify "
"the difference from an estimate based on formal charges."

#: ../../solid/polarization.rst:22
msgid "Berry位相・Wannier中心による分極の表し方の概要と、分極の差を求める経路が絶縁体を保たなければならない理由を説明する。"
msgstr ""
"Outline the representation of polarization in terms of the Berry phase and Wannier centers. "
"Explain why a path used to calculate a polarization difference must remain insulating."

#: ../../solid/polarization.rst:27
msgid "周期結晶の分極と分極の量子"
msgstr "Polarization and the Polarization Quantum in Periodic Crystals"

#: ../../solid/polarization.rst:29
msgid ""
"有限の分子なら、電気双極子モーメントは電荷と位置の積の和で一意に決まる。周期結晶で同じように 単位胞の中の電荷の双極子を体積で割ると、単位胞の取り方によって値が変わる "
"[Spaldin2012]_。 電荷 :math:`\\pm e` のイオンが間隔 :math:`a/2` で交互に並ぶ1次元の鎖（格子定数 :math:`a`）で確かめる。 "
"胞の左端を原点にして、:math:`-e` が :math:`a/4`、:math:`+e` が :math:`3a/4` にある胞を選ぶと、長さあたりの双極子は"
msgstr ""
"For a finite molecule, the electric dipole moment is uniquely determined by the sum of the "
"products of charge and position. Applying the same procedure to a periodic crystal and dividing "
"by the volume gives a result that depends on the choice of unit cell [Spaldin2012]_. Consider a "
"one-dimensional chain with ions of alternating charge :math:`\\pm e` spaced at intervals "
":math:`a/2`, with lattice constant :math:`a`. Choose the left edge as the origin and place "
":math:`-e` at :math:`a/4` and :math:`+e` at :math:`3a/4`. The dipole moment per unit length is"

#: ../../solid/polarization.rst:34
#, python-brace-format
msgid "P=\\frac1a\\left(-e\\cdot\\frac a4+e\\cdot\\frac{3a}4\\right)=\\frac e2"
msgstr "P=\\frac1a\\left(-e\\cdot\\frac a4+e\\cdot\\frac{3a}4\\right)=\\frac e2"

#: ../../solid/polarization.rst:38
msgid ""
"で、:math:`+e` が :math:`a/4`、:math:`-e` が :math:`3a/4` にある胞を選ぶと :math:`P=-e/2` になる。両者の差 :math:`e` "
"は、 電荷 :math:`e` を1格子定数だけ動かしたときの双極子の変化である。電子を隣の胞の同じ位置へ移しても結晶は変わらないので、 :math:`P` "
"はこの整数倍だけ不定である。3次元では、格子ベクトル :math:`\\boldsymbol R` と単位胞の体積 :math:`\\Omega` を使って"
msgstr ""
"Choosing a cell with :math:`+e` at :math:`a/4` and :math:`-e` at :math:`3a/4` gives "
":math:`P=-e/2`. The difference :math:`e` is the change in the dipole moment per unit length when "
"charge :math:`e` moves by one lattice constant. Moving an electron to the equivalent position in "
"the neighboring cell leaves the crystal unchanged, so :math:`P` is defined only modulo this "
"difference. In three dimensions, for a lattice vector :math:`\\boldsymbol R` and unit cell volume"
" :math:`\\Omega`, the corresponding quantity is"

#: ../../solid/polarization.rst:42
#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\boldsymbol P_{\\mathrm q}=\\frac{e\\boldsymbol R}{\\Omega}"
msgstr "\\boldsymbol P_{\\mathrm q}=\\frac{e\\boldsymbol R}{\\Omega}"

#: ../../solid/polarization.rst:47
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"を\\ **分極の量子**\\ と呼ぶ（スピンが縮退した系では2倍を単位にすることも多い）。分極の値は :math:`\\boldsymbol P_{\\mathrm q}` の "
"間隔で並ぶ集合（分極の格子）をなす。"
msgstr ""
"This is the \\ **polarization quantum**\\ . For spin-degenerate systems, twice this value is also"
" commonly used as the unit. The possible polarization values form a lattice with spacing "
":math:`\\boldsymbol P_{\\mathrm q}`, called the polarization lattice."

#: ../../solid/polarization.rst:50
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"一方、陽イオンを陰イオンに対して :math:`d` だけずらしたときの変化は、どちらの胞を選んでも :math:`\\Delta P=ed/a` で同じになる。 "
"実験で測るのも変化である。分極を電場で :math:`+P_{\\mathrm s}` から :math:`-P_{\\mathrm s}` へ反転させると、 電極の単位面積あたり "
":math:`2P_{\\mathrm s}` の電荷が外部回路を流れ、報告される自発分極はその半分である [Spaldin2012]_。 正方晶BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ の "
":math:`c` 軸方向（:math:`\\Omega=a^2c`）では :math:`P_{\\mathrm q}=e/a^2\\simeq1.0\\ "
"\\mathrm{C/m^2}=100\\ \\mu\\mathrm{C/cm^2}` で、 自発分極の実験値 :math:`26\\ \\mu\\mathrm{C/cm^2}` "
"[Wieder1955]_ の約4倍である。計算で分極を求めるときは、反転対称な参照構造から "
"原子を少しずつ動かして、同じ枝の上で変化を追う。一度に大きく動かすと、値が量子の分だけ別の枝へ跳んでも区別できないからである。 "
"この経路の途中の構造は、どれもバンドギャップの開いた絶縁体でなければならない（\\ :ref:`Berry位相による分極<fo-berry-phase>`）。"
msgstr ""
"Displacing the cation relative to the anion by :math:`d` gives the same change :math:`\\Delta "
"P=ed/a` for either choice of cell. Experiments likewise measure a change. When an electric field "
"reverses the polarization from :math:`+P_{\\mathrm s}` to :math:`-P_{\\mathrm s}`, a charge "
":math:`2P_{\\mathrm s}` per unit electrode area flows through the external circuit. The reported "
"spontaneous polarization is half of this value [Spaldin2012]_. Along the :math:`c` axis of "
"tetragonal BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\  (:math:`\\Omega=a^2c`), :math:`P_{\\mathrm q}=e/a^2\\simeq1.0\\ "
"\\mathrm{C/m^2}=100\\ \\mu\\mathrm{C/cm^2}`, roughly four times the experimental value of the "
"spontaneous polarization, :math:`26\\ \\mu\\mathrm{C/cm^2}` [Wieder1955]_. In a calculation, "
"displace the atoms in small steps from an inversion-symmetric reference structure and track the "
"change along the same branch. If the atoms are moved too far in one step, a jump of the value by "
"one quantum onto another branch cannot be detected. Each intermediate structure along the path "
"must remain insulating with an open band gap (see \\ :ref:`Berry-Phase Polarization <fo-berry-"
"phase>`)."

#: ../../solid/polarization.rst:61
msgid "反転対称な構造の分極"
msgstr "Polarization in Inversion-Symmetric Structures"

#: ../../solid/polarization.rst:63
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"反転は分極の向きを逆にするので、反転対称な構造では、分極の格子が反転で自分自身に移る。分極の値は :math:`\\boldsymbol P_{\\mathrm q}` "
"の整数倍だけ不定なので、条件は :math:`\\boldsymbol P\\equiv-\\boldsymbol P`\\ （:math:`\\boldsymbol P_{\\mathrm "
"q}` を法として） となり、分極の格子は0か、分極の量子の半分 :math:`\\boldsymbol P_{\\mathrm q}/2` を含む "
"[VanderbiltKingSmith1993]_。 上の交互イオン鎖は反転対称で、分極の格子は :math:`\\pm e/2,\\ \\pm3e/2,\\ldots`、すなわち量子 "
":math:`e` の半分の奇数倍である。 どちらの場合も、反転対称な構造は自発分極をもたない。測られる自発分極は、反転対称な参照構造から "
"極性の構造まで連続的に変形したときの分極の変化だからである。分極の値の不定性は、表面の束縛電荷が 表面の終わり方で変わることに対応する "
"[VanderbiltKingSmith1993]_。上の鎖では、端を :math:`-e` のイオンで終えるか :math:`+e` のイオンで終えるかで、端に現れる電荷が変わる。"
msgstr ""
"Inversion reverses the polarization. In an inversion-symmetric structure, the polarization "
"lattice must therefore map onto itself under inversion. The polarization is defined modulo "
"integer multiples of :math:`\\boldsymbol P_{\\mathrm q}`, so :math:`\\boldsymbol "
"P\\equiv-\\boldsymbol P`\\  (modulo :math:`\\boldsymbol P_{\\mathrm q}`). The lattice thus "
"contains either zero or half the polarization quantum :math:`\\boldsymbol P_{\\mathrm q}/2` "
"[VanderbiltKingSmith1993]_. The alternating ionic chain above has inversion symmetry, and its "
"polarization lattice is :math:`\\pm e/2,\\ \\pm3e/2,\\ldots`, the odd multiples of half the "
"quantum :math:`e`. Neither type of inversion-symmetric structure has spontaneous polarization. "
"The measured spontaneous polarization is the change along a continuous deformation from an "
"inversion-symmetric reference structure to a polar structure. The ambiguity in the polarization "
"corresponds to a dependence of the bound surface charge on the surface termination "
"[VanderbiltKingSmith1993]_. In the chain, the charge at the end depends on whether the "
"terminating ion has charge :math:`-e` or :math:`+e`."

#: ../../solid/polarization.rst:75 ../../solid/polarization.rst:115
msgid "Born有効電荷"
msgstr "Born Effective Charge"

#: ../../solid/polarization.rst:77
#, python-brace-format
msgid "原子 :math:`\\kappa` を :math:`\\beta` 方向へ :math:`u_{\\kappa\\beta}` だけ動かしたときの分極の変化の割合を"
msgstr ""
"The rate of change of polarization when atom :math:`\\kappa` moves by :math:`u_{\\kappa\\beta}` "
"in direction :math:`\\beta` gives"

#: ../../solid/polarization.rst:79
msgid ""
"Z^*_{\\kappa,\\alpha\\beta}=\\frac{\\Omega}{e}\\left.\\frac{\\partial P_\\alpha}{\\partial "
"u_{\\kappa\\beta}}\\right|_{\\boldsymbol E=0}"
msgstr ""
"Z^*_{\\kappa,\\alpha\\beta}=\\frac{\\Omega}{e}\\left.\\frac{\\partial P_\\alpha}{\\partial "
"u_{\\kappa\\beta}}\\right|_{\\boldsymbol E=0}"

#: ../../solid/polarization.rst:84
msgid ""
"と書き、\\ **Born有効電荷**\\ と呼ぶ。微分は、巨視的な電場を0に保ち、セルの形と大きさを固定して、原子 :math:`\\kappa` だけを 動かしたときのものである "
"[GhosezMichenaudGonze1998]_。動いた原子の電荷だけでなく、変位に伴って流れる電子の寄与も含む。 :math:`Z^*` "
"が変位によらないとみなせる範囲では、反転対称な参照構造からの変位で分極は"
msgstr ""
"This quantity is the \\ **Born effective charge**\\ . The derivative is taken with the "
"macroscopic electric field set to zero and the cell shape and size fixed, while only atom "
":math:`\\kappa` moves [GhosezMichenaudGonze1998]_. It includes both the charge on the displaced "
"atom and the electronic charge that flows in response to the displacement. Over the range in "
"which :math:`Z^*` can be treated as independent of displacement, the change in polarization from "
"an inversion-symmetric reference structure is approximately"

#: ../../solid/polarization.rst:88
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\Delta P_\\alpha\\simeq\\frac{e}{\\Omega}\\sum_\\kappa\\sum_\\beta "
"Z^*_{\\kappa,\\alpha\\beta}\\,u_{\\kappa\\beta}"
msgstr ""
"\\Delta P_\\alpha\\simeq\\frac{e}{\\Omega}\\sum_\\kappa\\sum_\\beta "
"Z^*_{\\kappa,\\alpha\\beta}\\,u_{\\kappa\\beta}"

#: ../../solid/polarization.rst:93
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"と見積もれる [GhosezMichenaudGonze1998]_。全原子を同じだけ動かしても分極は変わらないので、:math:`\\sum_\\kappa "
"Z^*_{\\kappa,\\alpha\\beta}=0` が成り立つ （電荷中性の和則）。そのため、どの原子を基準に変位を測っても :eq:`fo-linear-polarization` "
"の値は変わらない。"
msgstr ""
"This linear estimate follows [GhosezMichenaudGonze1998]_. A rigid displacement of all atoms "
"leaves the polarization unchanged, so :math:`\\sum_\\kappa Z^*_{\\kappa,\\alpha\\beta}=0` (the "
"charge neutrality sum rule). Consequently, the value from Equation :eq:`fo-linear-polarization` "
"is independent of the atom chosen as the reference for measuring displacements."

#: ../../solid/polarization.rst:96
msgid ""
"立方晶BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ では、BaとTiのサイトは立方対称なので :math:`Z^*` はスカラーになる。酸素のサイトは正方対称なので、 "
"変位がTi–O–Tiの鎖に沿う場合（O∥）と垂直な場合（O⊥）の二つの値をもつ。:numref:`tbl-born-charges-batio3` に、 第一原理計算の値を形式電荷と並べる。"
msgstr ""
"In cubic BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ , the Ba and Ti sites have cubic symmetry, so :math:`Z^*` reduces to "
"a scalar. The oxygen sites have tetragonal symmetry, giving one value for displacements along a "
"Ti–O–Ti chain (O∥) and another for perpendicular displacements (O⊥). :numref:`tbl-born-charges-"
"batio3` compares the values from first-principles calculations with the formal charges."

#: ../../solid/polarization.rst:100
msgid "立方晶BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ のBorn有効電荷（LDAの線形応答計算、:math:`a_0=3.94` Å [GhosezMichenaudGonze1998]_）"
msgstr ""
"Born effective charges in cubic BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\  (LDA linear response at :math:`a_0=3.94` Å "
"[GhosezMichenaudGonze1998]_)"

