msgid ""
"Born有効電荷で求めた約 :math:`29\\ \\mu\\mathrm{C/cm^2}` は、実験値 :math:`26.3\\ \\mu\\mathrm{C/cm^2}` "
"[Wieder1955]_ に近く、 形式電荷では約6割にとどまる。とくにO∥の寄与は、形式電荷では約3分の1になる。この構造のO∥の :math:`z` 座標は "
"分率で0.016、その標準不確かさは0.005なので、O∥の項は約3割変わりうる。Ghosezらは、Born有効電荷が変位とともに変わることを考慮し、 Hewatの実験の変位から "
":math:`28.6\\ \\mu\\mathrm{C/cm^2}` を得ている [GhosezMichenaudGonze1998]_。"
msgstr ""
"The estimate using Born effective charges, about :math:`29\\ \\mu\\mathrm{C/cm^2}`, is close to "
"the experimental value of :math:`26.3\\ \\mu\\mathrm{C/cm^2}` [Wieder1955]_. The formal charges "
"give only about 60% of the experimental value. In particular, they give about one-third of the O∥"
" contribution. The fractional :math:`z` coordinate of O∥ in this structure is 0.016 with a "
"standard uncertainty of 0.005, so its contribution can vary by about 30%. Ghosez and colleagues "
"accounted for the variation of the Born effective charges with displacement and obtained "
":math:`28.6\\ \\mu\\mathrm{C/cm^2}` from Hewat’s experimental displacements "
"[GhosezMichenaudGonze1998]_."

#: ../../solid/polarization.rst:202
msgid "解釈と限界"
msgstr "Interpretation and Limitations"

#: ../../solid/polarization.rst:204
msgid ""
":eq:`fo-linear-polarization` は、:math:`Z^*` が一定とみなせる変位の範囲で使える。BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ ではTiのBorn有効電荷が "
"変位とともに変わるので [GhosezMichenaudGonze1998]_、精度が要る場合は、参照構造から同じ枝の上でBerry位相の差を求める。 "
"原子の部分電荷（Löwdin電子数など）と変位の積を足しても、Born有効電荷を使った値にはならない。計算した分極は、計算で得た 変位の大きさを通じて、\\ :ref:`交換相関汎関数"
"<exchange-correlation-functional>`\\ や格子定数の選び方にも依存する。"
msgstr ""
"Equation :eq:`fo-linear-polarization` applies over the range of displacements for which "
":math:`Z^*` can be treated as constant. In BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ , the Born effective charge of Ti "
"varies with displacement [GhosezMichenaudGonze1998]_. When accuracy matters, use the Berry phase "
"to find the difference from the reference structure along the same branch. Summing the products "
"of atomic partial charges, such as those derived from Löwdin electron populations, and "
"displacements gives a different quantity from the result using Born effective charges. The "
"calculated polarization also depends on the choice of \\ :ref:`exchange–correlation functional "
"<exchange-correlation-functional>`\\  and lattice constants through their effect on the "
"calculated displacements."

#: ../../solid/polarization.rst:209
msgid "分極の量子を法とした不定性は、分極の差や、反転対称な参照構造からの変化を求めれば消える。計算プログラムが出力する 分極の値そのものは、どの枝の値かを確かめてから使う。"
msgstr ""
"The ambiguity modulo the polarization quantum cancels when calculating differences in "
"polarization or changes from an inversion-symmetric reference structure. Before using the "
"absolute polarization reported by a program, identify the branch to which it belongs."

